.research/agents/tdense15_report.md:288:PROVED exact two-value classification: all nonprincipal lambda(gamma) are Galois conjugates in the real cyclotomic field. Two distinct values have equal multiplicities, since every fiber of the Galois orbit has the same stabilizer size. Trace and Parseval then force the two values to be (-1+sqrt(q))/2 and (-1-sqrt(q))/2. Thus K=(1+sqrt(q))/2. This verifies the Paley spectrum assertion in NOTEBOOK 18.5; it is a verification of the lead's observation, not this round's discovery.
